{"id": "3.3-00460", "case_id": "t3.5.s1p.1b3270563d2c1892c5a7.rhs_2924b61db0ce75ed", "parent_id": "t1.3.s1p.1b3270563d2c1892c5a7", "source": null, "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Round-trip: Stage 1 → generated text → Stage 2</h2><div class=\"stage-grid\"><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 1</div><h3>Write the whole-module specification</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>Clean module RTL: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00460&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>stage1/design.v</a></td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Describe the interface, parameters, and observable behavior of this clean design. Return a self-contained specification, not RTL implementation code. A separate isolated call will receive your specification.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00460&amp;file=stage1%2FTASK.md'>stage1/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Generated whole-module specification (prose).</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage1/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00460&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module mg_01348(output wire [7:0] reg_0x03);\nassign reg_0x03=8&#x27;h00; \n endmodule</pre></details></div><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 2</div><h3>Repair the module</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>The generated Stage 1 text plus buggy mutant rtl: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00460&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>stage2_template/design.v</a>. Required top module: mg_01348.</td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Repair the functional fault in design.v using the specification and retained RTL context. Return the complete corrected RTL with the same top module. Only the default configuration is scored.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00460&amp;file=stage2_template%2FTASK.md'>stage2_template/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Complete repaired RTL module.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage2_template/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00460&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module mg_01348(output wire [7:0] reg_0x03);\nassign reg_0x03=~(8&#x27;h00); \n endmodule</pre></details></div></div><div class=\"flow\"><strong>Stage 1 output → abstraction gate → fresh Stage 2 input.</strong> The intermediate text is generated separately for each model/attempt. It is not a prefilled golden description. Stage 2 receives neither the clean RTL nor the Stage 1 conversation.</div><h2>Private final evaluation</h2><div class=\"card\"><table><tbody><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Reference RTL</th><td><a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00460&amp;file=private%2Fgolden.v'>private/golden.v</a></td></tr><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Score / oracle</th><td>Binary formal equivalence to the hidden clean module</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"muted\">The formal oracle consumes the complete Stage 2 RTL file and compares it with the clean reference. A golden RTL file is scoring material, not a generated Stage 1 output.</p></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/25e3e8eec2a402fe89e3c761bfa6da8241f1e8bbcda9998a038b5f0648b253a8.txt", "size": 4487, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "private/equivalence.ys", "url": "assets/7e233b5dfd8819f4aca1e82ee2cddd1540f03fa810f68bed729f0a3c82656da0.txt", "size": 595, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/golden.v", "url": "assets/1b3270563d2c1892c5a797e4bc5f5ae47b3f7e962b0edaabac41dfa28e7352a3.txt", "size": 79, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/negative/equivalence.ys", "url": "assets/7e233b5dfd8819f4aca1e82ee2cddd1540f03fa810f68bed729f0a3c82656da0.txt", "size": 595, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/negative/golden.v", "url": "assets/1b3270563d2